What it does: The exact opposite of an A record—it maps an IP address back to a domain name (Reverse DNS lookup).

The Analogy: Caller ID on your phone. When a number calls, your phone looks up the number to confirm the caller's business name.

sneakerhub.com Setup: Configured on your hosting provider's network for IP 198.51.100.25:

Plaintext
25.100.51.198.in-addr.arpa.    3600    IN    PTR    mail.sneakerhub.com.
Result: When your server sends an email, the recipient's mail filter does a reverse lookup on the sending IP. If the PTR record matches mail.sneakerhub.com, it passes anti-spam checks.
